<title>UK: Recycling Services makes AIM debut.</title>
<headline>Recycling Services makes AIM debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Recycling Services Group Plc, a specialist metals recycler, set a premium on their first day of trading on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Thursday.</p>
<p>By 1155 GMT the shares were quoted at 97-1/2p. They were placed at 90p in an issue valuing the company at 14.6 million stg and raising 3.6 million stg.</p>
<p>The proceeds of the float will mainly go to finance the acquisition of G&amp;P Batteries Ltd, allowing the group to move into lead recycling.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
</text>
